WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.880
After months of speculation, and a recent leak&nbsp;
that sent fans into a frenzy, the "Spider-Man:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:06.800
No Way Home" trailer is finally here.

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:10.240
From what we've seen so far, the film wastes&nbsp;
little time in addressing Peter Parker's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:14.480
less-than-ideal situation following the events of&nbsp;
"Spider-Man: Far From Home," in which everyone's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:19.040
favorite superhero was framed for the death of&nbsp;
Mysterio and outed to the world as Spider-Man.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.880
Lost and seeking answers, Tom Holland's&nbsp;
Peter Parker turns to Doctor Strange,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:26.960
played by Benedict Cumberbatch, who makes&nbsp;
a massive, universe-colliding mistake.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:31.360
Using a spell to wipe everyone's minds and thus&nbsp;
make them forget that Peter Parker is Spider-Man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:35.440
the Sorcerer Supreme accidentally contorts&nbsp;
the multiverse in the worst way imaginable.

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:40.160
A host of recognizable Spidey foes from previous&nbsp;
continuities enter the Marvel Cinematic Universe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:45.120
for the first time, ranging from Willem Dafoe's&nbsp;
Green Goblin from 2002's "Spider-Man" to Jamie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:49.360
Foxx's Electro from "The Amazing Spider-Man&nbsp;
2." That's a tall order for the novice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:53.440
Avenger and the protector of the Sanctum&nbsp;
Sanctorum, but luckily, they may have help.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.200
Though the rumored Tobey Maguire and Andrew&nbsp;
Garfield's Spider-Man incarnations have yet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:00.160
to appear in any promos, some&nbsp;
viewers believe they've spotted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:03.840
another fan-favorite hero in the "No Way&nbsp;
Home" teaser. Let's break down who it is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.880
and how they may fit into the&nbsp;
story, should they actually turn up.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:07.920
"Are you a public defender?"

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:08.640
"Uh, no."

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:13.360
Despite being pinned as Mysterio's murderer,&nbsp;
it doesn't appear as though Peter Parker is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:16.320
going on the run. Instead, as the&nbsp;
"No Way Home" trailer indicates,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:19.520
Parker is cooperating with law enforcement&nbsp;
to get to the bottom of this case,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:23.520
maintaining his innocence all the while.&nbsp;
Nevertheless, he can't win this fight alone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:26.800
meaning he will need someone to give&nbsp;
him a hand in court. Who better to do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:31.200
so than Marvel's own Matt Murdock, better&nbsp;
known by his vigilante alias, Daredevil.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:35.200
A whole army of other Twitter users have pointed&nbsp;
out that Charlie Cox's take on Daredevil,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:39.200
made famous by the beloved Netflix series,&nbsp;
could be hiding in plain sight throughout&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:42.240
the "No Way Home" trailer. There are&nbsp;
multiple shots of Peter Parker sitting in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:46.080
an interrogation room with what appears to&nbsp;
be a legal counsel of his own by his side,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:50.480
slamming his hands down on the table. Curiously,&nbsp;
the person's face is strangely omitted every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:53.680
time they're on screen. Of course, when&nbsp;
he's not cleaning up Hell's Kitchen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:58.160
Matt Murdock is a full-time lawyer, so his&nbsp;
involvement in Peter's case isn't too far-fetched.

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:01.520
It's also worth noting that Spider-Man and&nbsp;
Daredevil work together all the time in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:05.280
the pages of Marvel Comics, meaning The Man&nbsp;
Without Fear could help out the web-slinger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:09.680
with his villain problems at the movies as well.&nbsp;
Nevertheless, Cox's involvement in the project&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:13.840
is still unconfirmed, but fans do have reason&nbsp;
to hope that their theories could be correct.

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:17.840
The possibility of Charlie Cox appearing as&nbsp;
Matt Murdock in "Spider-Man: No Way Home"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:22.000
is both exciting and not exactly a surprise.&nbsp;
There’s been quite a bit of speculation about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:26.480
Cox being integrated into the larger MCU but&nbsp;
also a slew of rumors about him appearing in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:30.400
"No Way Home." For instance, in December&nbsp;
2020, there were early rumors pointing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:34.480
to Cox making an appearance in the next&nbsp;
"Spider-Man" movie. Then in January 2021,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:39.360
ComicBook.com reported that Cox had allegedly&nbsp;
wrapped filming for his role in that project.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:43.440
"Hearsay. Can't print any of it&nbsp;
without corroboration, can you?"

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:48.480
And the trail of breadcrumbs doesn't stop there.&nbsp;
There was a fresh round of speculation in July&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:52.960
2021 surrounding the fact that Cox was canceling&nbsp;
gigs at the same time that the "No Way Home"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:57.200
reshoots were scheduled to take place. There have&nbsp;
also been rumors that Cox is gearing up to appear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:02.080
in multiple upcoming MCU projects, including&nbsp;
"She-Hulk" and "Echo." If those rumors are true,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:06.480
it's easy to think that the hotly anticipated "No&nbsp;
Way Home" could make for a perfect reintroduction.

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:09.840
And that's not all. According to Variety,&nbsp;
when the deals were inked to bring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:14.000
live-action versions of Marvel characters&nbsp;
like Daredevil and Jessica Jones to Netflix,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:18.160
there was allegedly a stipulation that those&nbsp;
characters could not appear in any other capacity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:21.680
until two years after the cancelation&nbsp;
of the Netflix shows they originated on.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:25.760
Matt Murdock, and his alias Daredevil,&nbsp;
passed that milestone at the end of 2020,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:30.160
which would seem to mean that Marvel Studios&nbsp;
is totally free to welcome him back to the MCU.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:35.360
We'll find out either way when "Spider-Man: No&nbsp;
Way Home" hits theaters on December 17, 2021.

